@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# Post attachments (CON-73 + CON-75). All endpoints require authentication —
# run "Login" from sessions/sessions.http first.
#
# Lifecycle:
#   1. Create a post (see posts/posts.http) and capture its id.
#   2. Upload one or more attachments via POST .../attachments — the server
#      streams the bytes to S3, decodes magic bytes to validate the MIME
#      (JPEG/PNG/WebP/GIF for images, application/pdf for PDFs), and
#      returns metadata + a short-lived presigned GET URL. PDF uploads
#      also render a first-page PNG thumbnail (best-effort) and return
#      a `thumbnail_url` alongside `presigned_url`.
#   3. Reorder via PATCH .../attachments/{id} with `{"position": N}`.
#   4. Delete via DELETE .../attachments/{id}.
#
# Hard upload caps: 50 MB for images, 100 MB for PDFs.
# Mutations are blocked with 409 once the parent post is `published`.
# When the parent post is deleted, attachments cascade automatically
# (including any PDF thumbnails).
#
# Set @postId after creating a post you want to attach files to. For the
# PDF examples, @postId should reference a LinkedIn post (carousel/document
# post type).

@postId = REPLACE_ME
# An IMG asset from the content bank (content-bank/*.http), for from-asset.
@assetId = REPLACE_ME

### Upload an image  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample.png
--boundary--

> {%
client.global.set("attachmentId", response.body.id);
%}

### Attach a content-bank image  [protected]
# No upload: the asset's stored bytes are EXIF-stripped into the post's own
# object. alt_text is optional — omit it to carry the asset's alt text over.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments/from-asset
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "asset_id": "{{assetId}}"
}

### Attach a content-bank image — non-image asset (expects 422)  [protected]
# Point @assetId at an MD/PDF/URL asset first.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments/from-asset
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "asset_id": "{{assetId}}",
  "alt_text": "Written for this post"
}

### List attachments for the post  [protected]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments
Accept: application/json

### Get a single attachment  [protected]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments/{{attachmentId}}
Accept: application/json

### Reorder — move attachment to position 2  [protected]
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments/{{attachmentId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "position": 2
}

### Reorder — negative position (expects 400)  [protected]
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments/{{attachmentId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "position": -1
}

### Delete the attachment  [protected]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments/{{attachmentId}}

### Upload — no file (expects 400)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary--

### Upload — unauthenticated (expects 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample.png
--boundary--

### Upload — unsupported media type (expects 415)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="doc.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

this is not an image; the server rejects on magic-bytes regardless of the filename
--boundary--

### Upload — to an unknown post (expects 404)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/no-such-post/attachments
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample.png
--boundary--

### Upload a PDF (LinkedIn carousel/document)  [protected]
# @postId must reference a LinkedIn post. Response includes:
#   - mime_type: application/pdf
#   - page_count: <int>
#   - thumbnail_url: presigned URL to the rendered first-page PNG
#     (best-effort; may be empty if pdftoppm is unavailable)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf
--boundary--

> {%
client.global.set("attachmentId", response.body.id);
%}

### Upload a PDF on Instagram (expects 201 with platform_validation soft warning)  [protected]
# Switch @postId to an Instagram post first. The upload still succeeds
# (CON-73 §2.4 soft pre-check) but the response carries a
# platform_validation entry with rule="pdf_not_supported".
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf
--boundary--

### Upload a malformed PDF (expects 400)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{postId}}/attachments
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="evil.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

%PDF-1.4
this looks like a pdf but isn't really one — server rejects on parse failure
--boundary--
